## Known Limitations & Live Testing Notes

Each entry in `segments` is populated by the same conversion code as the
singular [`identitynow_segment_v1` data source](../data-sources/segment_v1.md) -
see its "Known Limitations & Live Testing Notes" section for the full list
of limitations shared by both.

`GET /segments/v1` has no `filters` query parameter (unlike some other
plural data sources in this provider, e.g. `identitynow_governance_groups_v1`) -
only `limit`/`offset` pagination is supported in this schema (the API's own
`count` query param, an X-Total-Count-header toggle, is intentionally
dropped from this schema entirely - `count` is a reserved root
attribute/block name in Terraform, matching `governance_groups_v1`'s
equivalent precedent). Filter client-side with a Terraform `for` expression
if you need a subset (see the example above).
